          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            There are at least two formalizations of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            is identified with a certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarized
            section) of a certain
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
          %p
            Here a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            is what is physics is called a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+function"} wave function
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+amplitude"} probability amplitude
            on the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            configurations. A choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            on this space is a choice of “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"}> canonical coordinates
            ” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"}> canonical momenta
            ”. Hence a polarized section, and hence a quantum state in the sense of geometric quantization, is, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            language, a
            = succeed "." do
              %em wave function of the canonical coordinates
          %p
            So the space of states is the subspace of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+sections"} space of sections
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            on those that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarized
          %p
            For details see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometric+quantization#QuantumStates"} geometric quantization – Space of quantum states
